@startuml strip-layout
' strip_layout(count, active, room): how the tab strip spends its room.
' Symbols: W window width, R room for tabs, n tab count, e equal share,
' a active width, o width of each other tab, k tabs shown (all in CSS px).
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #DDEBF7
  BorderColor #52687A
  ArrowColor #52687A
  FontColor #182734
}
title The tab strip: widths, icon-only tabs, and the "+N" window

start
:Room for tabs: strip padding, the gap, and the new-tab button come off
<latex>R = W - 2 \cdot 8 - 4 - 30</latex>; <<#DDEBF7>>
:Equal share, at most 200 px each, with 2 px between tabs
<latex>e = \min\left(200,\ \frac{R - 2\,(n-1)}{n}\right)</latex>;
if (e at least 128?) then (yes)
  :every tab is <latex>e</latex> wide; <<#E2EFDA>>
  stop
endif
:The active tab keeps 128 px; the others share the rest
<latex>a = 128, \qquad o = \frac{R - 128 - 2\,(n-1)}{n-1}</latex>; <<#FFF2CC>>
if (n at most 1, or o at least 44?) then (yes)
  :all <latex>n</latex> tabs show; <<#E2EFDA>>
  stop
endif
:Room left after the "+N" chip (44 px and its gap)
<latex>R' = R - 44 - 2</latex>; <<#FCE4D6>>
:As many tabs as fit at the minimum widths
<latex>k = 1 + \left\lfloor \frac{R' - 128}{44 + 2} \right\rfloor</latex>; <<#FCE4D6>>
:window = visible_window(n, active, k)
centred on the active tab, clamped to the ends; <<#FCE4D6>>
:split the <latex>k</latex> tabs as above, in <latex>R'</latex>; <<#FCE4D6>>
:the chip reads <latex>+(n-k)</latex> and opens the Tabs panel; <<#FCE4D6>>
stop

note right
  <b>Titles.</b> A tab <latex>w</latex> px wide fits its title to
  <latex>w - 66</latex> when active (padding 16, borders 2,
  icon 14, two 7 px gaps, close button 20), and to
  <latex>w - 39</latex> otherwise: an inactive tab's close
  button overlays the title on hover. A tab whose
  fitted title is empty or "…" shows only its icon.
end note
@enduml
